<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786030302254-13bf1f9b76.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p2">EA Sports has released <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition/id6755553408" rel="noopener noreferrer">Madden NFL 27 Arcade Edition</a>, a version of the popular football simulation franchise that Apple Arcade subscribers can play on the iPhone, iPad, Mac, and Apple TV. It’s a big release built specifically to take advantage of Apple hardware, allowing players to play the game on a wide variety of hardware.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786029847414-d3da2a70b0.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p4">I was struck by how easy it is to pick up and play the game whether you’re a diehard NFL fan or not. I don’t follow football closely, but I was able to get the hang of the game and have fun right away, knocking out a Quick Play match when I had a few minutes to spare.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786029964406-09c40ef9fa.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p6">Quick Play tightly limits the overall time it takes to complete a matchup, but it doesn’t sacrifice depth in the process. There are long lists of plays you can run, including suggested plays, play types, formations, and recents, as well as a wide variety of statistics. And after a big play, you can replay it with total control over the camera angle, too.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786029992739-bbe4494e4d.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p8">However, if you want to go really deep, the game’s Franchise Mode lets you play a full NFL season, managing your team all the way through the playoffs. You can also draft your dream team from the game’s huge catalog of real-world NFL stars. Plus, during the real-world NFL season, player attributes shift based on their actual performance.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786029934024-59895d2f26.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p10">Madden NFL 27 also looks terrific. The 120Hz playback is smooth on the iPhone, where I spent most of my time with the game, and even nicer on a bigger screen like my 14” M4 Max MacBook Pro, making for an immersive experience.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/06/shortcut-upload-1786029903942-ef9cb138a8.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p12">What impresses me most about Madden NFL 27, though, is how well it makes use of the Apple hardware and technologies at its disposal. Too often, those sorts of details get left behind when a big release is published on Apple platforms.</p>
<p id="p13">To its credit, EA has done an excellent job adapting Madden NFL 27 for Apple Arcade subscribers. You can play across every device mentioned above, leaving off on one device and picking up on another seamlessly because saves sync across devices. Every device supports game controllers and touch where applicable, and those devices with 120Hz displays support that, too.</p>
<p id="p14">Madden NFL 27 Arcade Edition <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition/id6755553408" rel="noopener noreferrer">is available now on the App Store as part of an Apple Arcade subscription</a>. The game is debuting on other platforms <a href="https://www.ea.com/games/madden-nfl/madden-nfl-27/faq" rel="noopener noreferrer">next week</a>.</p>
